ty","url":"https://eliastaylor.com/noexploit/","score":18,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"hailey","user_is_author":false,"tags":["php","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/zpcnmo","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/zpcnmo/there_isn_t_easy_exploit_for_this_php"},{"short_id":"was9lk","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:28:49.122-05:00","title":"Three configurable prettyprinters (2023)","url":"https://reasonableapproximation.net/2023/08/10/three-configurable-prettyprinters.html","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"abhin4v","user_is_author":false,"tags":["haskell"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/was9lk","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/was9lk/three_configurable_prettyprinters_2023"},{"short_id":"azc9ip","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:13:24.569-05:00","title":"Two Welsh organisations reprimanded after cyber-attack exposed children’s information","url":"https://ico.org.uk/about-the-ico/media-centre/news-and-blogs/2026/10/password1-is-not-an-appropriate-password/","score":-2,"flags":4,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"ettolrach","user_is_author":false,"tags":["security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/azc9ip","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/azc9ip/two_welsh_organisations_reprimanded"},{"short_id":"nbd1cs","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:09:55.509-05:00","title":"Garmin Revamps and Opens Up Connect Developer API Program","url":"https://www.dcrainmaker.com/2026/10/garmin-connect-api-revamps-connect-developer.html","score":12,"flags":1,"comment_count":1,"description":"\u003cp\u003eNot exactly related to programming, but as a Garmin user I've always wanted an API for personal access so I can make my own stuff on top of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI also \u003cem\u003ereally\u003c/em\u003e like the fact that they have a tier specifically targeting \u003cem\u003epersonal\u003c/em\u003e use. My prediction and fear is that, with AI allowing people to code their own apps, companies will become \u003cem\u003emore\u003c/em\u003e jealous of the data they collect (even though it's not theirs, of course). So seeing Garmin going in the opposite direction makes me happy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDirect link to the program: \u003ca href=\"https://developer.garmin.com/gc-developer-program/overview/\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://developer.garmin.com/gc-developer-program/overview/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Not exactly related to programming, but as a Garmin user I've always wanted an API for personal access so I can make my own stuff on top of it.\r\n\r\nI also *really* like the fact that they have a tier specifically targeting *personal* use. My prediction and fear is that, with AI allowing people to code their own apps, companies will become *more* jealous of the data they collect (even though it's not theirs, of course). So seeing Garmin going in the opposite direction makes me happy.\r\n\r\nDirect link to the program: https://developer.garmin.com/gc-developer-program/overview/","submitter_user":"pscanf","user_is_author":false,"tags":["api"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nbd1cs","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nbd1cs/garmin_revamps_opens_up_connect"},{"short_id":"hplfis","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:45:58.884-05:00","title":"examining the macOS gcc binary","url":"https://zoey-on-github.github.io/blog/macgcc.html","score":48,"flags":0,"comment_count":13,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"juliethefoxcoon","user_is_author":true,"tags":["mac","reversing"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hplfis","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hplfis/examining_macos_gcc_binary"},{"short_id":"dcvs3u","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:15:07.575-05:00","title":"Announcing DuckDB 2.0.0 LTS “Cinnamon Teal”","url":"https://duckdb.org/2026/10/21/announcing-duckdb-200.html","score":20,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"